            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"the-haystack\">The haystack</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>3,000,265 characters</strong> of generated chronicle. Three facts are\nplanted far enough apart that no single read catches two of them:</span>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>fact</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">offset</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">position</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>hop1 (Bhama Shah)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">450,938</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">15.0%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>hop2 (Chavand)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,352,555</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">45.1%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>hop3 (1597)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,554,757</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">85.2%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Task \u2014</strong> After the battle of Haldighati, a minister restored Maharana Pratap's finances with a personal donation. Name the capital Pratap founded with those funds, and the year he died there.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The chain: <em>the minister</em> \u2192 <strong>Bhama Shah</strong> \u2192 <em>the capital he funded</em> \u2192\n<strong>Chavand</strong> \u2192 <em>the year Pratap died there</em> \u2192 <strong>1597</strong>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Hop 2's search term does not exist until hop 1 returns. You cannot embed a\nquery for \"the capital founded by the minister whose name you don't know\nyet\" \u2014 which is why this is recursion and not retrieval.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">There's a trap in hop 1: the chronicle spells it <code>Bhama Shah</code> (two words), so\ngrepping the modern <code>Bhamashah</code> returns zero hits.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
